# EcoFleet: disable the stock SWUpdate suricatta daemon.
#
# swupdate.service is the upstream daemon that polls a hawkBit/suricatta server
# (the stock config points at a nonexistent varupdate:8080). EcoFleet does not
# use it — OTA runs entirely through gobi-agent's one-shot `swupdate -i <bundle>
# -f /etc/swupdate/ecofleet.cfg`. Left enabled it only ever surfaces as a failed
# unit at boot ("provide a public key file"), so turn it off in the image.
#
# This file's "10-" prefix sorts before the recipe's own 98-swupdate.preset, so
# for swupdate.service this "disable" is the first match and wins. swupdate.socket
# has no line here and falls through to 98-swupdate.preset (left as-is).
disable swupdate.service
